<$TOP/mkfiles/mkfile.proto

# the goken cross-toolchain itself: used by tests/ (mk objtype=riscv64) and,
# once self-hosting is viable, as CC/AS/LD for the top-level build too.
# The RISC-V (rv64) lineage. ja/jc/jl are the *same*
# binaries as ia/ic/il (assemblers/ia/mkfile, compilers/ic/mkfile,
# linkers/il/mkfile install them under both names); their main()s
# auto-select thechar='j' (64-bit) from argv[0]'s basename (or, for
# ia/il, a -j flag too), the original inferno 'i'/'j' dual-width riscv
# convention -- there is no separate top-level arch letter for riscv64
# the way arm64 got its own '7' distinct from arm's '5'. Object ext .j.
O=j
CC=jc
LD=jl
AS=ja
AR=iar

CFLAGS=$CFLAGS_COMMON -I$TOP/include/arch/riscv64

# see mkfiles/386/mkfile's own ARCHEXTRAOFILES comment. No vlop.$O
# entry needed here (64-bit-native, no software vlong emulation), but
# setjmp.s is still needed on every arch, this one included.
ARCHEXTRAOFILES=arch/riscv64/setjmp.$O
